Fork provenance
---------------
- Fork base: upstream commit `f467033`
  ("Merge pull request #32 from johnhom1024/feat/browser-pairing-device-subprotocol"),
  package version `0.11.1`. `f467033` is an ancestor of the snapshot below;
  nothing from upstream main after `f467033` is included.
- Snapshot content: package version `0.12.2` — six commits on top of `f467033`,
  listed in the next section.
- Versioning: this repository restarts at `1.0.0` and does not follow upstream's
  `0.x` numbers. It starts from a single clean initial commit: upstream history
  is not carried over, so `git log` here is not a substitute for upstream history.

Changes relative to upstream `f467033` (included in this snapshot)
------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Workspace rename and delete frames — `workspace-rename` / `workspace-delete`
   requests, the `workspace-manage-v1` capability, and proxying of the host's
   `workspace/rename` and `workspace/delete`.
2. Replay of pending questions when a device connects later — a device that
   joins after a question was raised still receives it.
3. `feat(host-api)`: whitelisted exact-route Host API proxy, **default off**.
   `hostApiPaths` allow-list, POST-only, loopback-only `?gateway=` shorthand,
   `host-api-proxy-v1` capability advertised only when the allow-list is
   non-empty. See `docs/host-api-proxy-spike.md`.
4. Docs: instructions for running the gateway against a second host profile.
5. `feat(wire)`: live `job/settled` carries tool/job identity and timing —
   `jobId` / `kind` / `label` / `toolCall` / `startedAt` / `finishedAt` /
   `status` / `cause` / `producerReported` / `detail`, using the same field names
   as the history side (duration = `finishedAt - startedAt`).
6. `feat(wire)`: live `job/registered` carries identity fields — `jobId` /
   `kind` / `label` / `toolCall{callId,rootCallId}` / `startedAt`, so a client
   can pair `jobId` with `toolCall.callId` structurally from the start of a job
   instead of parsing a shell tool's kickoff text.

Both wire additions are purely additive: a client that ignores them keeps
working unchanged.

Upstream contribution that is already inside the fork base
----------------------------------------------------------
- Browser pairing device subprotocol (`dsh-device.<id>` / `dsh-device-name.<name>`
  in the `Sec-WebSocket-Protocol` list, so a plain browser needs no custom
  header to pair) was contributed upstream by this fork's author as PR #32 and
  merged as `f467033`. It is therefore part of the base, not part of the delta.

Fork-only housekeeping (no protocol change)
-------------------------------------------
- Package renamed `dsh-plugin-mobile-gateway` -> `dsh-host-gateway`, version
  reset to `1.0.0` (1.0.1 renames the browser client module id to match the
  package name; keeping the upstream id caused a duplicate-factory boot failure
  when both packages were present), repository / homepage / bugs point at this fork.
- `cordis.patch.yml`: the bundle `name` follows the package rename; the row `id`
  stays `mobile-gateway`, because profile patches address the row by id.
- Added this NOTICE, `MIGRATION.md`, and the attribution section at the top of
  README.

Intentionally NOT renamed
-------------------------
The wire protocol (`dsh-mobile-v1`, `hello.protocol = 3`), the bundle row id
(`mobile-gateway`), the on-disk management MARKER, and log/error prefixes that
mention `mobile-gateway` are left untouched on purpose: they are protocol,
on-disk and identity strings that clients, logs and existing installs already
refer to.

The browser client module id is *not* in this list any more: 1.0.1 renamed it to
`dsh-host-gateway`. Leaving the upstream id registered while the old package was
also installed made DSH's client-module graph reject the boot with
`duplicate factory registration`. See `MIGRATION.md` section 7.
